  "summary": "Unbounded memory use on large request bodies",
  "details": "The `graphql()` and `graphql_sync()` functions of `juniper_hyper` read the whole body of a POST request into memory before they parsed the body. The functions had no limit on the size of the body. A client could thus send a large body and exhaust the memory of the server. The request needs no authentication.\n\n`juniper_hyper` 0.10.1 reads at most 2 MiB of a request body by default. The functions respond with `413 Payload Too Large` to larger bodies. A `juniper_hyper::BodyLimit` in the extensions of a request changes the limit for the request.",
  "severity": [
    {
      "type": "CVSS_V3",
      "score": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"
